---
import BioPage from '../../components/BioPage.astro';

// Wording is carried over from the live page. Changes from the live page, for Bryn's review:
//  - "Glen Allen" became "Richmond" (the footer and offices list Richmond).
//  - The two "Virginia Bar Association Top Attorney Award" lines are left out: no year, source
//    unknown, and the owner's rule is "experienced", not "top". Add back only if Bryn confirms them.
//  - Award and association logos (Best Law Firms, Super Lawyers, a "1 million" badge) are left out:
//    they were files from the old paid theme and need dates and permission to use.
//  - Oct 28, per Bryn: the Virginia Lawyers Weekly and Super Lawyers mentions are out until documented,
//    and marketing claims ("hundreds and hundreds" of cases, "first-class ... second to none") are
//    reworded to checkable facts.
//  - The sidebar said "Cum Laude" for Randolph-Macon while the biography says "magna cum laude";
//    the sidebar now matches the biography. Bryn to confirm.
//  - Oct 31 SEO rewrite: career facts from Bryn (licensed 2011; former prosecutor with the Virginia
//    Office of the Attorney General; claimant and defense firms; Pathfinder since 2019; thousands of
//    comp cases; hundreds of mediations). No hearing count: Bryn doesn't have one.
const title = 'Bryn Swartz, Virginia Workers’ Comp Lawyer | Pathfinder';
const description =
  'Bryn Swartz, licensed in Virginia since 2011, has handled thousands of workers’ comp cases on both sides before founding Pathfinder Injury Law.';
const facts = [
  {
    heading: 'Experience',
    items: [
      'Licensed in Virginia, 2011',
      'Former prosecutor, Virginia Office of the Attorney General',
      'Workers’ comp for injured workers and for employers and insurers',
      'Founded Pathfinder Injury Law, 2019',
    ],
  },
  {
    heading: 'Education',
    items: [
      'B.A. Randolph-Macon College (Magna Cum Laude, Phi Beta Kappa)',
      'J.D. University of Richmond School of Law (Magna Cum Laude, Walter Scott McNeill Law Honor Society)',
    ],
  },
  { heading: 'Associations', items: ['Virginia State Bar', 'Virginia Trial Lawyers Association'] },
];
---
<BioPage
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path="/bryn-swartz/"
  name="Bryn Swartz"
  role="Owner & Attorney"
  photo="/images/photos/bryn.jpg"
  photoAlt="Bryn Swartz, owner and attorney at Pathfinder Injury Law"
  facts={facts}
>
  <p class="lead">
    Bryn Swartz is a Virginia workers’ compensation lawyer and the owner of Pathfinder Injury Law in
    Richmond. He has been licensed in Virginia since 2011 and has handled thousands of workers’ comp
    cases, first at firms on both the injured worker’s side and the insurance company’s side, and
    since 2019 at Pathfinder, where he represents only people hurt at work in Virginia.
  </p>

  <h2 id="experience">Experience</h2>
  <p>
    Bryn started his career as a prosecutor with the Virginia Office of the Attorney General,
    prosecuting online crimes against children. He then moved into workers’ compensation, working at
    firms that represented injured workers and at firms that defended employers and their insurance
    companies.
  </p>
  <p>
    He has handled thousands of
    <a href="/virginia-workers-comp-lawyer/">Virginia workers’ compensation</a> cases through every
    stage: filing claims, discovery, hearings before the Commission, and review appeals. He has taken
    part in hundreds of mediations to settle them. His years on the defense side mean he has seen from
    the inside how insurance companies and their lawyers evaluate a claim, from the first
    <a href="/insurance-recorded-statement/">recorded statement</a> to the
    <a href="/workers-comp-settlement-in-virginia/">settlement</a> offer.
  </p>

  <h2 id="pathfinder">Why He Started Pathfinder</h2>
  <p>
    Bryn was laid off from a claimant-side law firm the day his son was born in 2019. He and his wife
    Mandy Truman founded Pathfinder sitting in the hospital room while Mandy was recovering from a
    C-section with a brand new baby boy, nothing to lose, and the whole world to gain. Pathfinder is a
    conscientiously small firm that handles only Virginia workers’ compensation, so every client gets
    diligent, attentive service in the middle of a work injury.
  </p>
  <p>
    Bryn does his work wearing shorts and a NORML or mountain biking tee shirt. He firmly disavows the
    fallacy that one must wear a suit or uncomfortable shoes or have a dumb, self-serious office to be
    a great lawyer and a fierce client advocate. He is well known amongst his peers as a diligent,
    resourceful, and…unconventional lawyer. He prefers to do his job while riding his beloved Yeti
    SB130 mountain bike lost in the woods on the side of a mountain somewhere.
  </p>

  <h2 id="about">About Bryn</h2>
  <p>
    Bryn was born and raised in Richmond, Virginia, the son of two musicians and schoolteachers. After
    dropping out of college to go on tour and make albums with his punk band, he resumed his education
    at Randolph-Macon College. He graduated in 2008 magna cum laude, in the top seven percent of his
    class, and with membership in the Phi Beta Kappa honor society. He then attended the University of
    Richmond School of Law, from which he graduated magna cum laude, in the top eleven percent of his
    class, and with membership in the Walter Scott McNeill Law Honor Society.
  </p>
  <p>
    He is a member of the Virginia State Bar and the Virginia Trial Lawyers Association. Outside of
    law, Bryn loves mountain biking, traveling, eating great food, hanging out with his family and
    dogs, being a coffee snob, playing drums, and listening to podcasts, audiobooks, and music. Meet
    the rest of the <a href="/about-us/">Pathfinder team</a>.
  </p>
</BioPage>
